# Feature Flow Per Stack Layer

When adding or updating an agent feature flow (book / cancel / modify / similar), implement **one layer at a time**. Do not mix orchestration into UI or presentation into Mastra.

## Ownership

| Order | Layer | Path | Owns |
|------:|-------|------|------|
| 1 | Mastra | `apps/agent/src/mastra` | Tools, schemas, prompts/playbook, `prepareStep` pins, mutation execute |
| 2 | CopilotKit HITL | `apps/web` `useHumanInTheLoop` | Confirm/cancel cards, `respond({ confirmed })` |
| 3 | CopilotKit mutation UI | `apps/web` `useRenderTool` | Headless notice → phase store; same HITL card phases |
| 4 | AG-UI | `apps/agent/src/ag-ui` | Stream/abort/transcript only when bridge is broken |

Mastra decides **what** happens. CopilotKit UI decides **how it looks**. AG-UI only **bridges**.

## Required sequence

```
HITL tool → user respond() → mutation tool → headless notice → same-card phase UI
```

- Mutation tools run only after HITL `confirmed: true`.
- UI must not call mutation tools directly.
- Retry = send a normal user message; agent chooses tools.
- Prefer headless mutation notices (`return null`); no second success card.
- Same-card phases: `review → submitting → success | failed | cancelled | expired`.
- Pass `parameters` into mutation notices for correlation-key matching (create/cancel/update).
- Prefer live Zustand outcomes; on history/refresh, derive success/failed from mutation tool results in `agent.messages` (presentation only — do not rewrite transcript).
- Keep tool **schemas** stable; update **descriptions** when the UI phase machine owns success/failure.

## Do not

- Put booking phase logic in AG-UI
- Rewrite transcript/memory in the UI for long-term fixes
- Expect a separate ConfirmSuccess / ToolSuccessNotice for create/cancel/update
- Bypass agent orchestration from Retry buttons
